    description: "The Civic Innovators Fellowship (CIF) is a free, virtual program offered by Civics Unplugged for current high school students and students whose gap year began immediately after the preceding school year. The 16-week fellowship runs from fall through early spring, with a break between its fall and spring portions. Participants study history, democracy, technology, and culture, examine their own sense of purpose, and apply material from the fellowship within their communities. Weekly lessons are held live on Monday evenings and are interactive and discussion-based. Attendance at these sessions is required. Fellows participate alongside a regional cohort of peers and alumni mentors. International students may apply, although the fellowship is conducted in English and its content and subsequent opportunities focus on the United States. After completing the fellowship, participants join the Civics Unplugged Community, which provides access to the organization’s network and funding opportunities. Fellowship completion also gives participants exclusive access to apply for Civics Unplugged’s in-person Civic Innovation Academies and its Civic Innovation Lab incubator. The Civic Innovation Academy is a free, one-week, in-person program offered by Civics Unplugged for alumni of its Civic Innovators Fellowship. Academies are held on university campuses in the United States and bring together approximately 25–75 Fellows to study civic innovation through location-specific issues. Current sites include Georgetown University in Washington, D.C., where participants address civic problems connected to the nation’s capital, and UCLA in Los Angeles, where topics include housing justice, climate action, and community-based innovation.",
