    url: "https://www.elon.edu/u/academics/access-and-success/elon-academy/about/",
    description: "Elon Academy is an intensive, three-phase college access and success program provided by Elon University. This program focuses on academic strengthening, leadership development, college-going knowledge and culture, service, and family involvement. The main objectives of the program are to inspire academically promising students to pursue higher education, build leadership skills, and develop a sense of social responsibility. The program is especially beneficial for students who are often underrepresented on college and university campuses. The program covers key topics like academic classes, co-curricular, service and cultural experiences, college planning, and college visits. It also emphasizes developing reading, writing, speaking, and critical thinking skills. The program further fosters collaborative, organizational, study, and time management skills. Additionally, it offers SAT preparation, college selection assistance, essay writing support, community service opportunities, and guidance on college grants and scholarships. The delivery of Elon Academy is a hybrid of online and in-person components. The in-person component involves three intensive 3-week summer residential experiences at Elon University prior to the 10th, 11th, and 12th grades, which mirror college life. The online component includes a monthly Saturday Academy during the academic year. The instructors for Elon Academy are a multigenerational and diverse faculty and staff from Elon University. These instructors serve as role models and provide regular contact and consistent support to scholars and their families. Scholars are paired with a College Access Team (CAT) Mentor —trained students from Elon University— who provide regular support and encouragement. For eligibility, the program is open to academically promising high school students in Alamance County with a financial need and/or no family history of college. It's important to note that scholars are encouraged to undertake a challenging high school curriculum, including honors and AP classes. Upon completion of the Elon Academy, participants will have gained the academic strengths, interpersonal skills, and sense of self-worth that will position them to succeed in college and beyond. They will also have developed a comprehensive understanding of college life and the college application process. Moreover, the program provides continuing support to Elon Academy graduates and their families to ensure college completion.",
