    description: "Project Green Challenge (PGC) by Turning Green is a month-long initiative designed to inform, inspire, and mobilize students around climate action, public health, social justice, and advocacy. Its main objective is to empower young leaders to enact change in their daily lives, on campuses, and within communities. Participants engage in daily challenges throughout October, each centered around a unique environmental theme such as food, water, zero waste, and carbon footprint. These challenges help students learn the benefits of eco-living through full immersion and provide tips and resources for reducing their carbon footprint and becoming leaders in their schools or communities. The program is delivered online, with participants completing challenges and sharing their progress via social media. At the end of the 30 days, up to fourteen finalists are selected to attend the PGC Finals in San Francisco, where they present their 30-day journeys and develop Climate Action Projects (CAPs). Finalists then work with mentors from December to April to implement their CAPs before presenting them virtually. The main benefits of participating include gaining a deeper understanding of climate and social justice issues, learning eco-friendly living practices, and developing leadership skills. Finalists also have the opportunity to compete for the $5,000 Acure Green Award.",
