    name: "STEM Research Academy (STEM RA)",
    org: "CUNY",
    category: "Program",
    field: "Medicine & Health",
    eligibility: null,
    location: "New York, NY",
    cost: "Free",
    cost_detail: "Free with a $1,000 stipend upon completion of summer research experience.",
    deadline: "2025-12-02",
    duration: null,
    url: "https://www.cuny.edu/academics/current-initiatives/k16/stem-research-academy/",
    description: "The STEM Research Academy (STEM RA) is a free, two-semester program for motivated New York City public high school students who want to explore science, technology, engineering, and mathematics while earning college credit. The program combines classroom learning with hands-on research, offering access to CUNY’s award-winning faculty and research facilities. Participants gain early exposure to scientific inquiry while building valuable experience for college and future careers. During the spring semester, students enroll in a pre-college research course that introduces the foundations of scientific investigation, data collection, and analysis. In the summer, they transition into a six-week research experience conducted in CUNY laboratories. Projects span a wide range of disciplines across participating campuses, such as psychology, molecular biology, computer science, mechanical engineering, urban ecology, and space science. The program culminates in a research exhibition at the American Museum of Natural History, where students present their findings alongside peers in the New York City Science Research and Mentoring Consortium. Instruction is led by CUNY faculty mentors who are experts in their fields and supported by undergraduate student mentors. Teaching emphasizes hands-on experimentation, collaboration, and critical thinking. Students also receive guidance on scientific writing and communication as part of their preparation for presenting research outcomes. Eligibility is open to highly motivated 10th and 11th grade NYC public school students, with select 9th graders considered individually. Participants receive a stipend and an MTA MetroCard upon completing both semesters. By the end of the program, students not only gain practical research experience and enhanced scientific literacy but also join a citywide network of STEM scholars, opening pathways to future research and mentorship opportunities. Here’s the list of CUNY campuses that host the STEM Research Academy and the types of research areas they offer: - Baruch College – Organizational Psychology, Plant Science, Fly Genetics - Brooklyn College – Animal Behavior, Learning and Memory, Urban Ecology, Environmental Science - John Jay College of Criminal Justice – Toxicology, Molecular Biology, Chemistry - LaGuardia Community College – Biology, Environmental Science - Lehman College – Psychology, Molecular Biology, Chemistry - New York City College of Technology (CityTech) – Air Quality Testing, Mechanical Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Computer Science - Queens College – Environmental Science, Ecology, Animal Science - Queensborough Community College – Space Science, Space Weather, Fiber Optics, Capacitor Building, Physics - The City College of New York (CCNY) – Acoustics (underwater communication), Cognitive Psychology, Parasitic Worm Research (invasive species) - York College – Engineering, Medical Psychology, Molecular Biology, Nursing",
