    description: "The Austin Public Library's Teen Volunteer Program is a seasonal opportunity designed for teenagers between the ages of 13 and 17. The program's primary objective is to involve youth in various library duties. These duties traditionally involve assisting the Youth Services librarians with tasks such as circulation, program planning, preparing programming materials, program set-up and take down, supervising and assisting participants during programs, re-shelving books, running specialized clubs for teens, and light cleanup tasks. The program runs for 10 weeks during the Fall (October-December) and Spring (March-May) seasons, during which volunteers are expected to work a 2-hour shift once per week. Over Summer (June-July), the program lasts 8 weeks and requires a commitment of a 4-hour shift once per week. The Teen Volunteer Program is in-person, with placements available at many Austin Public Library locations. To be eligible for the program, applicants must be within the stipulated age bracket by the start of the season. Applicants must complete an online application, be available for an interview with the volunteer coordinator, accept a placement offer, complete a successful background check, attend a mandatory youth volunteer orientation, and commit to volunteering with a maximum of two absences during the program season. Through the Teen Volunteer Program, participants will gain valuable experience in a professional environment, learn the inner workings of a library, and develop skills such as teamwork, organization, and communication. These skills will prove beneficial for their personal growth and future career prospects.",
