    description: "The Oakland Youth Poet Laureate (OYPL) program, provided by the Oakland Public Library, is a citywide initiative aimed at celebrating literacy and empowering young poets in Oakland. It seeks to recognize and support talented writers aged 13-18 by offering them a platform to showcase their poetry and connect with broader opportunities. Participants in the program are encouraged to submit their poems, which are evaluated anonymously in the first round based on content, craft, and voice. The program includes a final round where finalists are judged on performance and leadership, with criteria including a letter of support, artist statement, awards, community service, and previous involvement in the OYPL program. This round requires a mandatory in-person reading and interview with a panel of judges in April. The program runs from June to June, and participants must complete the full year to receive awards. The Oakland Youth Poet Laureate, who scores the highest, receives a $5,000 educational scholarship, while finalists receive a $500 prize. To participate, applicants must meet age requirements, reside locally, and not attend college full-time in the year following high school graduation. The program offers substantial benefits, including public speaking support from the Oakland Public Library staff and connections to other youth and writing organizations. It is designed to enhance participants' leadership skills, writing abilities, and public presence, ultimately aiming to elevate youth voices in the community.",
