    description: "The College LAUNCH for Leadership Program, provided by Wake Forest University, is a nine-month initiative focused on college preparation, social consciousness, and leadership development. The program aims to equip scholars with the skills and knowledge necessary to pursue their individual goals and serve humanity. Through exposure to various careers and discussions about academic excellence, equitable rights, and influential leadership, participants are prepared to act as catalysts for change within their communities. The curriculum is delivered through monthly Saturday Summits from September to May, supplemented by ongoing mentorship and guidance for all scholars and alumni. Participants are engaged in Youth Participatory Action Research, where they work in groups to explore a social justice issue of their choice. This provides scholars with the opportunity to develop their research skills, understand complex factors contributing to social injustices, and equip themselves as leaders to make an impact on their communities. The program is managed by a team of experienced professionals from Wake Forest University's Pre-College Programs. These include Assistant Vice President and Executive Director Kyla Hollingsworth, who holds a BA and MBA from Point Park University, and Director Betsy Schneider, who has a BA from Bucknell University and an MAT from the University of North Carolina at Charlotte. Program Manager Mackenzie Wilkins, holding a BA from Wake Forest University and an MS from the University of North Carolina at Greensboro, also contributes to the program's operation. Eligibility for the program is not explicitly stated, but it is clear that the program is designed for high school juniors in Winston-Salem, Charlotte, and surrounding communities. However, the program is not a pipeline to Wake Forest University, and participation does not guarantee admission to the university. The application process begins in January. Upon completion of the College LAUNCH for Leadership Program, scholars are expected to be prepared for college, have developed a critical understanding of social injustices within their communities, and have further developed their leadership skills. Moreover, LAUNCH alumni have gone on to attend over 70 colleges and universities across the country, promoting social justice and equity. In 2022, LAUNCH alumni were awarded over $15 million in college scholarships and grants.",
