    url: "https://www.americaontech.org/tech-flex-leaders.html",
    description: "America On Tech (AOT) offers free, multi-stage programs that introduce high school students to technology skills and careers, with a structured pathway from first exposure through internships and early career support. The high school pathway begins with TECH360, a three-week summer bootcamp focused on the fundamentals of artificial intelligence and core computing concepts, and continues with Tech Flex Leaders (TFL), a nine-month, hybrid after-school program for juniors and seniors in New York City, Los Angeles, Atlanta and Miami. Instruction is led by industry professionals and supported by mentors, with a blend of lectures, workshops, hands-on projects, and peer collaboration. The curriculum builds progressively. TECH360 emphasizes AI literacy and problem-solving through guided lessons and projects. TFL deepens skills with weekly technical training and professional development, followed by a Demo Day in the fall and a specialized track in the spring, such as: - Advanced Web Development (HTML, CSS, frameworks) - UX Design - Digital Marketing - Product Management - Data Science AI concepts and tools are threaded throughout each track. Sessions run on weekday late afternoons/early evenings during the school year, primarily online with periodic in-person orientations, showcase events, and milestone activities. AOT programs serve high school students ages 16–18, with TFL available to those enrolled in eligible city regions. Prior coding experience is not required. Participation requires a consistent weekly commitment and willingness to attend a limited number of in-person sessions each term. Instruction is delivered by Certified/In-Industry professionals, with additional guidance from near-peer mentors who support project work and skill development. Graduates gain portfolio projects, applied technical skills, and career readiness training. TFL participants connect with professionals during career days and mentorship events and, for qualifying students, can access paid summer internships through AOT’s employer network (with the strongest placement pipeline in New York). After high school, alumni remain engaged through AOT’s network, including job and internship matching (Access Tech), paid peer-mentor roles, and targeted skills fellowships—extending support into college and early career.",
