    url: "https://espr.camp/",
    description: "The European Summer Program on Rationality (ESPR) is a comprehensive 10-day immersive workshop designed for mathematically talented students aged 16 to 19 who are eager to understand themselves and the world through applied rationality. Located in Somerset, UK, the program runs from August 21st to 31st. It is free for all admitted students, including tuition, room, and board, with travel scholarships available. The main objective is to equip participants with rigorous, quantitative skills and a versatile toolbox of concepts and techniques useful in various aspects of life. The curriculum covers a diverse range of topics such as game theory, cryptography, mathematical logic, AI safety, styles of communication, and cognitive science. Key classes include practical applications of Bayes' theorem, understanding personal and professional bottlenecks, and critically analyzing persuasive rhetoric. The program also encourages participants to design and run their own content, fostering creativity and leadership. ESPR is delivered in-person and features a mix of optional classes each day, complemented by student and staff-organized activities. The program emphasizes interaction among participants and the enriching atmosphere, which alumni often highlight as its most valuable aspect. Renowned intellectuals, such as Scott Aaronson and Anders Sandberg, have participated as speakers in past sessions, enriching the learning experience with diverse perspectives. The program is led by a team of experienced instructors with diverse qualifications. Gavin Leech, with a PhD in AI from Bristol, serves as the Camp Lead. Jan Kulveit, with a background in AI alignment, acts as the Executive Director. Other instructors include Julia Brodsky, a former NASA astronaut instructor, and Tomas Gavenciak, a researcher in game theory and bounded rationality. The teams varied expertise ensures a rich learning environment for participants. ESPR aims to enhance participants' decision-making skills and understanding of the world, providing them with the knowledge and confidence to apply rational thinking in real-world scenarios. The program also fosters a community of like-minded individuals passionate about mathematics, philosophy, and cognitive sciences.",
