    description: "The Product Management: An Introduction course, offered by IBM, provides a foundational entry point into the fast-paced world of product development and strategy. Designed specifically for beginners and currently ranked a 4.6 out of 5, the program explores how product managers drive success by balancing user needs, business goals, and technical constraints. Participants will gain a high-level overview of the end-to-end product lifecycle, learning how to transform market insights into value-driven products that resonate with global audiences. The curriculum is delivered through five specialized modules that blend theoretical knowledge with practical application. Learners begin by defining the essential roles and competencies of the profession before diving into the \"Product Management Body of Knowledge\" (ProdBoK®). Key modules cover critical topics such as cross-functional collaboration, value propositions, and product strategy. The course culminates in a final project where students apply their skills to simulated real-world scenarios, ensuring they understand how to manage personas, conduct SWOT analyses, and oversee product growth. Instruction is provided by industry experts from IBM, including Matt Versdahl and Rav Ahuja, who bring decades of experience in global technology and digital transformation. This course serves as the first installment in the IBM Product Management Professional Certificate, allowing learners to build a stackable credential. Upon finishing the approximately 10 hours of material, participants earn a shareable certificate from IBM to showcase their job-ready skills on LinkedIn and other professional networks.",
