    url: "https://youthcouncil.lacity.gov/",
    description: "The Olivia Mitchell LA City Youth Council, established by the City of Los Angeles, offers a citywide cohort where 30 selected youth serve a one-year term. These youth from across the city get an opportunity to learn about the local government's inner workings, drive community projects, civic events, and make policy and budget recommendations to elected and civic leaders. They aim to improve the well-being, safety, and accomplishment of young Angelenos. The council's mission is to speak truth to power, identify bold solutions, and transform communities positively and enduringly. The LA City Youth Council is overseen by the City’s Youth Development Department (YDD) and Department of Neighborhood Empowerment (EmpowerLA). It honors the legacy of Olivia Mitchell, a public servant who has inspired countless government and community leaders over several decades with her passion for mentoring young Angelenos. The council members are involved in creating a citywide Youth Development Strategic Plan, promoting equity and inclusion, and fostering an environment where youth feel ownership and accountability over policy framework and initiatives. The opportunity allows members to develop skills that would help them in their future career and life. They also receive financial compensation for their active participation as council members. This council operates both virtually and in person, with members expected to attend meetings twice monthly and participate in other special youth council activities. Eligibility to apply requires applicants to be between 16 to 25 years old, live within the City of Los Angeles boundaries, and provide one to two references. The application opens annually, and selected members are expected to contribute to improving programs, policies, and practices affecting young people in the City, partner with community organizations, civic leaders, and other youth leaders, and receive training and leadership development from City partners on a wide range of issues. Through their participation, members assist in drafting and presenting recommendations on various issues related to youth development, including City budgets and policies.",
