    description: "The Maimonides Health Scholars program, offered by Maimonides Emergency Medicine, provides high school juniors and seniors, as well as college students, with an immersive experience in the Emergency Department (ED) of Maimonides Medical Center, a large teaching hospital in Brooklyn, New York. This unpaid internship aims to introduce students to the healthcare field and the principles of clinical medicine, making it ideal for those considering careers as physicians, nurses, nurse practitioners, physician assistants, physical therapists, psychologists, social workers, or paramedics. Participants in the program will engage in various activities, including assisting in patient care, improving communication with patients, and supporting ED staff. They will rotate through different areas of the ED and gain firsthand exposure to the operations of a busy urban emergency department. Interns will also have the opportunity to participate in ongoing ED research projects, provided they complete an additional training module. The program is delivered in-person, with several rotation periods throughout the year: April 1st to June 30th, June 16th to September 1st (Summer), September 2nd to January 4th (Fall), and January 5th to April 5th (Winter). Applications are reviewed on a rolling basis. Eligibility requires submission of application forms, a brief essay or video, documentation of vaccination status, a letter of recommendation, and participation in a 15-minute virtual interview. Accepted applicants will undergo further processing as volunteers, which includes an in-person interview and a mandatory 3-hour orientation. Through this comprehensive program, participants will gain valuable insights and experience that are foundational for a career in healthcare.",
