    description: "Rising Stars Youth Leadership Academy is an academically enriched program provided by the City of Fort Worth. Focusing on leadership training, the program equips youth aged 13 to 17 years with critical life skills and problem-solving abilities. The aim is to prepare participants for careers in diverse fields such as civic/community engagement and leadership. Through interactive sessions, the program educates participants about community issues and career opportunities. It encourages interaction with both emerging and established leaders in Tarrant County, contributing to a broader understanding of the community and the working world. In addition, participants are guided to analyze their personal strengths and weaknesses, set vocational goals, and develop self-esteem. Emphasis is placed on building resilience and the ability to overcome challenges. The academy is a year-round program and participants can re-apply each year. A notable component of the curriculum includes field trips designed to complement classroom learning. These excursions provide practical exposure and help connect students with employers, businesses, and government officials. Participants also have the opportunity to enhance their professional and personal etiquette, public speaking, networking, and technology skills. Upon completion of the program, each student receives a certificate of leadership and community service recognition. This recognition not only validates their learning but also serves as a valuable addition to their academic and professional profiles. The academy, therefore, not only imparts leadership skills but also prepares students for future educational and career paths.",
