    description: "The Frontline Volunteer opportunity at the Asian Art Museum offers a unique learning experience in Asian art and culture. The program primarily focuses on enhancing the museum experience for visitors and contributing to the museum's operations. Frontline volunteers either assist at the information desk and coat check or in the Cha May Ching Museum Boutique. At the information desk, volunteers guide visitors to locations and activities of interest, while those in the museum boutique provide customer service and help visitors find merchandise related to the museum's collections and exhibitions. The program offers an array of benefits including unlimited free admission to the museum, access to the museum’s research library, and discounts in the museum boutique and cafe. Volunteers also receive invitations to exclusive volunteer-only tours and events. This program is in-person and requires volunteers to handle visitor's backpacks and bags, suggesting some periods of standing. The program is open to individuals from diverse communities, backgrounds, and age groups, from high-schoolers to retirees. No previous experience or expertise in Asian art is required. Volunteer applications are accepted at all times. There is a mention of a mandatory orientation session/interview post-application, held at least twice a month. For those applying for the summer months, they must apply by May and volunteer more frequently than twice a month during summer. The main outcomes of this volunteer program include a deeper understanding of Asian art and culture, customer service skills, and the satisfaction of contributing to the operations of a valued art museum. This program is also a great opportunity to meet new people and interact with visitors from around the world.",
