    description: "The DoSeum Volunteer is a learning opportunity that gives individuals the chance to serve the museum and its visitors. This program allows volunteers to help children learn through play, share their unique talents, develop new skills, and explore career options in the museum industry. Participants can earn academic credit or community service hours while expanding their personal and professional networks. Additionally, volunteers receive a discount at The DoSeum Store and Café. The program is delivered in-person, with volunteers being asked to commit to at least one shift of service per month for a minimum of six months. Each shift typically lasts 2-3 hours. The program is open to individuals aged 11 and up, with different provisions for those under 14. For instance, volunteers aged 11-13, referred to as Junior Doers, must be accompanied by an adult or chaperone. In addition to the General Program, The DoSeum offers a special High School Program called \"Discovery By Doing\". This program allows high school students to earn over 150 hours towards the President Service Award. Participants will complete a minimum total of 100 hours of volunteer service during the school year and 50 hours during the summer months. The training covers facilitation and engagement practices, STEM model activities, detailed exploration, and knowledge of The DoSeum galleries, hands-on activities, and presentations. It also includes reflection/goal setting and professional development skills such as leadership skills and college prep. All volunteers, regardless of the specific program, are required to attend a New Volunteer Orientation and Emergency Preparedness Training before starting their service. The orientation includes information about The DoSeum's COVID-19 procedures. As a result of this learning opportunity, participants can expect to acquire new skills, gain valuable work experience, and make a positive impact on their community.",
