    description: "The ACE Mentor Program of Greater NY is a free, year-long after-school mentorship program designed to expose high school students to careers in architecture, construction, and engineering. The program runs from November through May and is delivered in a team-based format, with each team comprising approximately 25 high school students and 15-20 mentors. These mentors, who are industry professionals from various fields including architecture, civil/structural engineering, mechanical/electrical engineering, and construction management, guide students through their respective career pathways, introduce them to foundational industry knowledge, and teach them to use design software commonly utilized in their everyday jobs. Following this introduction to basics, teams work on a mock design project of their choice as a practical application of what they've learned. This project is then presented in Spring to other teams, ACE GNY staff, and industry leaders. The program also offers students a deep understanding of the design and construction industry, a firsthand look at professional environments and office life, connections to alumni and professionals for ongoing support and networking, introduction to college programs and degree requirements, access to construction sites, opportunities for scholarships, internships and post-college employment, and training in presentation and team-building skills. Mentors, who are vital to implementing the program's mission, guide their students through hands-on activities and the development of a team design project. They gain an altruistic sense of \"giving back,\" the gratification that comes with sharing knowledge and wisdom with eager students, networking opportunities, and chances to enhance presentation, leadership, and other professional skills. ACE Greater NY teams meet after school at industry firms for at least 15 sessions throughout the year, adhering to the New York City Department of Education school calendar. To participate in the ACE GNY program, students must first register and then will receive information about selecting the team they would like to join. Students are welcome to join ACE GNY throughout their high school years, and scholarships are available to senior students who apply and qualify.",
