    description: "The Young Scholars Program (YSP) at Northeastern University provides high school students with a distinctive opportunity to engage in hands-on research within the fields of science and engineering. Designed for rising seniors who have completed their junior year, this free program allows participants to work in research laboratories across the Colleges of Engineering, Science, and Health Sciences. Students collaborate with faculty on diverse projects, such as exploring active particles in flow with Professor Sara Hashmi, designing model compression algorithms with Professor Shelley Lin, optimizing battery chemistries with Professor Mike Kane, or evaluating cancer therapies with Professors Mansoor Amiji and Lara Milane. This exposure to cutting-edge research offers a practical introduction to scientific inquiry and innovation. Beyond laboratory work, the program enriches students’ experiences through a variety of educational and professional development activities. Participants attend a special seminar series, Introduction to Engineering, featuring presentations from professors and graduate students on topics like radar, superconductivity, and robotics. The program also includes field trips to corporate and government sites, such as Biogen and the U.S. Army Natick Soldier Systems Center, where students observe engineers in action. Additionally, students receive college and career counseling from program coordinators and mentors, gain access to university facilities like Snell Library, and experience college life, all of which contribute to a well-rounded understanding of scientific and engineering careers.",
