    description: "The You Be The Chemist Challenge, provided by the Chemical Educational Foundation (CEF), is a free STEM-based competition aimed at students in grades 5-8. Its main objective is to celebrate science and promote interest in STEM careers by engaging students in a fun and collaborative environment. Participants work in teams of three to four to answer timed questions and create videos proposing innovative solutions to community-based challenges. The competition is structured in multiple levels, with Regional Challenges leading to State and ultimately a National Challenge. Key topics and skills covered in the Challenge include chemistry concepts, problem-solving, teamwork, and communication. The competition encourages students to explore scientific concepts and sustainability issues, fostering an understanding of chemistry's role in everyday life and its impact on society. The Challenge is delivered both in-person and virtually, depending on the availability of Regional Challenges in participants' areas. In-person Regional Challenges run from mid-January to early March, while virtual Regional Challenges are available for teams without a nearby in-person event. The National Challenge takes place in person in Houston, TX, in June. The competition begins with registration in early October, and teams have until late December to register. Video submissions are due by March 21, and the combined scores from Regional Challenges and video evaluations determine the State Winners. The top five state-winning teams advance to the National Challenge, where they present their solutions to a panel of judges and compete for scholarships. The Challenge offers participants the opportunity to develop critical thinking, collaboration, and presentation skills, while also providing exposure to STEM fields and potential scholarships for winners.",
