    description: "The City College of New York’s STEM Institute is an academic enrichment organization that encourages under-represented minority middle and high school students to realize their academic potential through educational programs at a collegiate level. The STEM Institute offers courses in physical sciences, mathematics, English, computer programming, engineering, and more. It also provides a select group of students with the opportunity to conduct research with faculty at The Grove School of Engineering. The ultimate goal of the institute is to encourage students to pursue careers in the fields of engineering, technology, science, business, and/or mathematics. The programs are offered both in-person and online, subject to student enrollment, and are structured to foster inclusivity and adaptability. The Institute uses creative and hands-on approaches in teaching to create an enriching learning environment. The After-School Program runs from 3:30 PM to 6:30 PM, twice a week, while the Saturday Program aims to bridge the gap between high school and university life by offering college-like courses in a campus setting. The STEM Institute is staffed by individuals passionate about igniting the curiosity of students and motivating them to pursue careers in the STEAM fields. The team comprises of lead instructors, teaching assistants, and tutors who are actively sought year-round for the Fall, Spring, and Summer Programs. Participation in the STEM Institute is entirely free, and the programs are designed to cater to students who reside in or study within Northern Manhattan and the greater expanse of New York City. The Institute's mission is to inspire, educate, and empower the next generation of innovators and problem solvers, guiding young minds toward a future where innovation and problem-solving are at the forefront in the world of STEM.",
